description:
Change the scene with up to 50 typed operations as ONE undo step. Everything is checked first (names, bones, aliases, expect, if_revision); a failure while applying restores what the batch changed. Result: what changed (before/after), created names, new revision. Without if_revision the batch applies to the document as it is now.
Refs are object names; an object created or copied earlier in the batch is "$alias" (its "as"), and a rename or delete is visible to the later operations. Rotations: {euler_deg:[x,y,z], order?} or {quaternion:[w,x,y,z]}, in the holder's own rotation mode. Colours are linear RGB.
set_transform {ref, location?, rotation?, scale?, delta?}; fit_height {ref, height?, ground?=true, ground_z?=0, children?=true, scale_axes?=z|uniform} (z stretches the height only; uniform keeps proportions); pose_bone {ref, bone, location?, rotation?, scale?}; aim_bone {ref, bone, target:{point}|{object, bone?}|{direction}, axis?=Y, tolerance_deg?} (reports error_deg);
insert_key {ref, bone?, paths:[location|rotation|scale], frame, interpolation?}; shift_keys {ref, bone?, paths?, frames?:[first,last], offset | delete:true} (moves or deletes keys);
create_object {kind:empty|camera|light|mesh|text, name, as?, primitive? size? (mesh: size is a cube's edge, a plane's side, a sphere's diameter, a cylinder's diameter and height; also a text's font size), light_type? energy? (light), lens? (camera), body extrude? align_x? align_y? (text), location?, rotation?, collection?, parent?};
duplicate {ref, as?, name?, suffix?, offset?, linked?=false, children?=true} (with its hierarchy); set_material {ref, material, color?, roughness?, metallic?, slot?} (creates the material when no material has that name);
scene_settings {frame_start?, frame_end?, frame_current?, fps?}; rename {ref, name}; delete {refs}; link|unlink {ref, collection}; create_collection {name, parent?}; set_parent {ref, parent? (omitted or null: unparent), bone?, keep_transform?=true};
add_marker {name, frame, camera?}; set_camera {ref}; add_constraint {ref, type:TRACK_TO|DAMPED_TRACK|COPY_LOCATION|COPY_ROTATION|CHILD_OF, target, subtarget?, name?}.
